WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.375
Here's what the check guards against,
from Chapter 08's dangers table.

2
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:09.507
Two systems updating one attribute
means drift that's fixed and recreated

3
00:00:09.507 --> 00:00:13.563
on every sync, forever; that's a
Finding, and an exit code of one.

4
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:16.617
Field names that differ
can hide a second writer,

5
00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:21.200
so the check would report no overlap;
the guard is the reviewed alias list.

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.388
A wrong directory name makes every attribute
look unwritten; the check refuses it.

7
00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:29.406
A disabled mapping counted
would give false findings,

8
00:00:29.406 --> 00:00:31.687
so disabled object mappings are skipped.

9
00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:35.725
And here's what it misses: writers
outside provisioning policies.

10
00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:37.638
A person has to confirm those.

11
00:00:37.638 --> 00:00:39.913
The guide is clear about scope, too.

12
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:41.550
The check reads exports.

13
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.516
It doesn't check approver
systems or lanes;

14
00:00:44.516 --> 00:00:47.380
those stay a manual validation of Gate 2.
